    "answer": {
      "short": "When a complete opposite side–angle pair is known and the cosine rule cannot be applied directly, for example with two angles and one side.",
      "worked": "With two angles and one side, find the third angle using the angle sum of a triangle. Then use the known opposite side–angle pair in the sine rule to find another side. There are insufficient known side lengths to apply the cosine rule directly.",
